;; compute-capacity-ontology — kotoba EAVT vocabulary for WORLDWIDE COMPUTING-CAPACITY growth
;; ADR-2606072000 · actor: kasa 嵩 (嵩 = bulk / volume / amount — the reckoner of the world's
;;                                  accumulating compute)
;;
;; PURPOSE
;;   A content-addressed Datom (EAVT) vocabulary that records, from PUBLIC information, the
;;   WORLDWIDE annual MAGNITUDE and GROWTH of computing capacity across four domains the
;;   founder named:
;;     (1) STORAGE      — HDD + SSD capacity SHIPPED per year (exabytes); installed base
;;     (2) MEMORY       — DRAM + NAND market revenue + bit-shipment growth
;;     (3) GPU / CPU    — discrete-GPU + client-CPU units shipped; datacenter-accelerator revenue
;;     (4) COMPUTE/FLOPS — TOP500 aggregate performance; frontier-model training compute (Epoch AI)
;;   plus DATACENTER total power capacity (GW) as the physical envelope. Each data point is one
;;   OBSERVATION (a series × a period × a value), linked to the PUBLIC SOURCE it came from. The
;;   lens is PLANNING + LABOR-LIBERATION compute-commons sizing (how much compute the world is
;;   adding, so the religious-corp can size its own non-rival compute donation against it) — NOT a
;;   market-research product, NOT a forecast, NOT a targeting / export-control list.
;;
;;   kasa is the COMPUTE-CAPACITY face of the observation upper layer: the industry-aggregate
;;   sibling of kanjō 勘定 (per-company 決算) and the demand-side counterpart of the silicon actors
;;   (iwakura / fuigo / tsukuru / handotai). Where kanjō asks "what did ONE company disclose?",
;;   kasa asks "how much compute did the WORLD add this year?".
;;
;; SOURCES (constitutional — G1): PUBLIC, redistributable headline figures + open datasets ONLY:
;;   - WSTS / SIA  global semiconductor sales (public monthly/annual press releases)
;;   - TrendForce / company press releases  DRAM + NAND market revenue, bit-shipment growth
;;   - IDC / company shipment reports  HDD + SSD exabytes shipped (public headline figures)
;;   - Jon Peddie Research (JPR)  GPU add-in-board unit shipments (public press summaries)
;;   - TOP500  aggregate Rmax (public list, semiannual)
;;   - Epoch AI  notable-models training-compute database (CC-BY, redistributable)
;;   - Our World in Data  (CC-BY) derived public series
;;   PROHIBITED inputs (Charter Rider §2(e) anti-gatekeeping + §2(c) vendor query-tracking, mirrors
;;   kanjō G1): the PAID, copyrighted FULL reports + subscription terminals of Gartner / IDC /
;;   Omdia / TrendForce / Bloomberg / S&P / Statista-Pro. The HEADLINE FIGURES those vendors put in
;;   free press releases are public and admissible; the VENDOR REPORT / TERMINAL COMPILATION is not.
;;   Read the press release + the open dataset, never the paywalled report.
;;
;; SUBSTRATE (ADR-2605262130 + 2605312345): canonical state is the kotoba Datom log. IPFS = block
;;   backend, MST = ingress/interop wire, Base L2 = trust anchor. NO RisingWave / SQL. Source CSV /
;;   PDF / dataset snapshots → DataLad → IPFS under 80-data/compute-capacity (NO git-lfs; G8); the
;;   source document CID is anchored on :compute.source/doc-cid.
;;
;; HISTORY / 非終末論 (ADR-2605192100 §1.15): a source REVISES a prior estimate (e.g. IDC restates
;;   last year's exabytes; Epoch AI re-estimates a model's training FLOP). kasa does NOT delete the
;;   prior observation — it asserts a NEW observation at a later transaction time and sets
;;   :compute.obs/superseded-by on the old one (forward pointer only; the original Datom stays).
;;   Read the truth "as-of" a date; there is no single final capacity number.
;;
;; SOURCING HONESTY (G5, mirrors kanjō / kabuto / tsumugi / watatsuna):
;;   :*/sourcing ∈ { :authoritative  ; parsed from a primary published report / dataset row (the
;;                                      figure mirrors the source verbatim)
;;                   :representative  ; a publicly-documented HEADLINE figure, ROUNDED — the bounded
;;                                      illustrative R0 seed, NOT the exact dataset row
;;                   :estimated       ; kasa ESTIMATED a present/past quantity from public proxies
;;                                      (gap-fill / nowcast of an UNREPORTED-but-knowable value);
;;                                      MUST carry :compute.obs/method describing how — NEVER a
;;                                      future forecast (that is mitooshi 見通し; see G4)
;;                   :synthesized }   ; DERIVED by kasa (a YoY / CAGR / aggregate); MUST be flagged,
;;                                      never presented as a reported figure
;;   Every observation, growth and aggregate carries an explicit sourcing keyword. The R0 seed is
;;   :representative (headline, rounded) with the FLOPS-training + datacenter-power rows :estimated.

{:schema/id      "compute-capacity-ontology"
 :schema/version "0.1.0"
 :schema/adr     "2606072000"
 :schema/note    "kotoba-native worldwide computing-capacity vocabulary for kasa 嵩. Industry-aggregate sibling of kanjō 勘定 (corporate-financials-ontology, ADR-2606032000) and demand-side counterpart of the silicon actors (handotai / iwakura / fuigo). Records measured/estimated ACTUALS + historical growth only — future forecasting is mitooshi 見通し (ADR-2606051800), deliberately out of scope (G4). Memory (:dram / :nand) is a SUBSET of :semiconductor revenue — kept in distinct domains so aggregates never double-count (see :compute.agg note)."

 :attributes
 [;; ── :compute.series/* — the DEFINITION of one measured series (what is being counted) ──
  {:db/ident :compute.series/id        :db/valueType :db.type/string  :db/unique :db.unique/identity :db/doc "stable id, e.g. \"cap.semi.revenue.world\" or \"cap.storage.hdd-capacity.world\""}
  {:db/ident :compute.series/domain    :db/valueType :db.type/keyword :db/doc ":semiconductor | :dram | :nand | :storage | :gpu | :cpu | :flops | :datacenter — the capacity domain (memory domains are a SUBSET of :semiconductor; see :compute.agg note — never sum across these)"}
  {:db/ident :compute.series/metric    :db/valueType :db.type/keyword :db/doc "what is measured: :revenue | :shipped-capacity (exabytes shipped/yr) | :shipped-units (devices/yr) | :bit-shipment-growth | :installed-base | :flops-installed (TOP500 Σ Rmax) | :flops-training (largest-model training compute) | :power-capacity"}
  {:db/ident :compute.series/unit      :db/valueType :db.type/keyword :db/doc ":usd | :bytes | :exabytes | :units | :flops | :watts | :ratio (dimensionless growth)"}
  {:db/ident :compute.series/scale     :db/valueType :db.type/keyword :db/doc ":ones | :thousands | :millions | :billions | :petaflops | :exaflops | :gigawatts — the multiplier on :compute.obs/value"}
  {:db/ident :compute.series/geography :db/valueType :db.type/keyword :db/doc ":world | :americas | :europe | :asia-pacific | :china | :jp | :us | … (the geographic scope of the series)"}
  {:db/ident :compute.series/label     :db/valueType :db.type/string  :db/doc "human label, e.g. \"Worldwide semiconductor sales / 世界半導体売上高\""}
  {:db/ident :compute.series/note      :db/valueType :db.type/string  :db/doc "scope / comparability caveat (e.g. \"discrete add-in-board GPUs only — excludes integrated\")"}
  {:db/ident :compute.series/sourcing  :db/valueType :db.type/keyword :db/doc ":authoritative | :representative | :estimated | :synthesized"}

  ;; ── :compute.obs/* — ONE observation (a series at a period = the EAVT-native capacity datum) ──
  {:db/ident :compute.obs/id           :db/valueType :db.type/string  :db/unique :db.unique/identity :db/doc "stable id, e.g. \"obs.cap.semi.revenue.world.2024\""}
  {:db/ident :compute.obs/series       :db/valueType :db.type/ref     :db/doc "→ :compute.series/id"}
  {:db/ident :compute.obs/year         :db/valueType :db.type/long    :db/doc "calendar year the observation covers (annual cadence)"}
  {:db/ident :compute.obs/value        :db/valueType :db.type/double  :db/doc "the magnitude, in :compute.series/scale units of :compute.series/unit. Scientific notation allowed (e.g. 5.0e25 for :flops :ones)"}
  {:db/ident :compute.obs/source       :db/valueType :db.type/ref     :db/doc "→ :compute.source/id (the public source this value came from)"}
  {:db/ident :compute.obs/method       :db/valueType :db.type/string  :db/doc "REQUIRED when :sourcing :estimated — how kasa derived the present/past estimate (the proxies + method). Empty for :representative / :authoritative reported rows"}
  {:db/ident :compute.obs/superseded-by :db/valueType :db.type/ref    :db/doc "→ :compute.obs/id of a later revision (when a source restated this value). FORWARD pointer only — the original Datom is RETAINED (非終末論; read as-of). Absent when never revised"}
  {:db/ident :compute.obs/sourcing     :db/valueType :db.type/keyword :db/doc ":authoritative | :representative | :estimated | :synthesized"}

  ;; ── :compute.source/* — a PUBLIC source (the provenance / admissibility anchor) ──
  {:db/ident :compute.source/id        :db/valueType :db.type/string  :db/unique :db.unique/identity :db/doc "stable id, e.g. \"src.sia\" / \"src.epoch\""}
  {:db/ident :compute.source/publisher :db/valueType :db.type/keyword :db/doc ":wsts | :sia | :trendforce | :idc | :gartner | :omdia | :jpr | :top500 | :epoch-ai | :our-world-in-data | :company-filing — the issuing org (G1 = public/redistributable HEADLINE or open dataset only, NEVER a paid full report / terminal compilation)"}
  {:db/ident :compute.source/title     :db/valueType :db.type/string  :db/doc "the public document / dataset title"}
  {:db/ident :compute.source/access    :db/valueType :db.type/keyword :db/doc ":press-release | :open-dataset | :public-list | :report-summary | :company-filing — the PUBLIC access channel used (never :paid-terminal / :subscription)"}
  {:db/ident :compute.source/license   :db/valueType :db.type/keyword :db/doc ":cc-by | :cc-by-sa | :public-domain | :press-release (free quotation of a headline figure) | :ogl — redistribution basis (G1/G8)"}
  {:db/ident :compute.source/url       :db/valueType :db.type/string  :db/doc "canonical public URL of the source"}
  {:db/ident :compute.source/retrieved :db/valueType :db.type/string  :db/doc "ISO-8601 date the figure was read (provenance; empty in the :representative seed)"}
  {:db/ident :compute.source/doc-cid   :db/valueType :db.type/string  :db/doc "IPFS CIDv1 of the archived source snapshot (DataLad-pinned under 80-data/compute-capacity; G8 no git-lfs). Empty in the :representative seed"}
  {:db/ident :compute.source/sourcing  :db/valueType :db.type/keyword :db/doc ":authoritative | :representative"}

  ;; ── :compute.growth/* — DERIVED YoY / CAGR (aggregate-first, :synthesized, G5-flagged) ──
  ;;   NEVER re-ingested as an observation. A measured rate of change, NOT a forecast (G4) or verdict (G2).
  {:db/ident :compute.growth/id        :db/valueType :db.type/string  :db/unique :db.unique/identity :db/doc "stable id, e.g. \"growth.cap.semi.revenue.world.2023-2024.yoy\""}
  {:db/ident :compute.growth/series    :db/valueType :db.type/ref     :db/doc "→ :compute.series/id"}
  {:db/ident :compute.growth/kind      :db/valueType :db.type/keyword :db/doc ":yoy (year-over-year, consecutive) | :cagr (compound annual growth rate over the span)"}
  {:db/ident :compute.growth/from-year :db/valueType :db.type/long    :db/doc "start year of the growth window"}
  {:db/ident :compute.growth/to-year   :db/valueType :db.type/long    :db/doc "end year of the growth window"}
  {:db/ident :compute.growth/value     :db/valueType :db.type/double  :db/doc "the growth rate as a fraction (e.g. 0.191 = +19.1%); :yoy = v[t]/v[t-1]-1, :cagr = (v[end]/v[start])^(1/years)-1"}
  {:db/ident :compute.growth/basis     :db/valueType :db.type/string  :db/doc "the obs ids the growth was derived from (audit trail for the :synthesized value)"}
  {:db/ident :compute.growth/sourcing  :db/valueType :db.type/keyword :db/doc "always :synthesized — kasa computed it; it is NOT a reported figure"}

  ;; ── :compute.agg/* — domain / geography AGGREGATE (aggregate-first output, G3) ──
  ;;   COVERAGE-HONEST: Σ is bounded by the series ingested in that (domain, unit), NOT a market
  ;;   total; read every aggregate against :compute.agg/n. Aggregation is ONLY within one
  ;;   (:domain × :unit) — memory (:dram / :nand) is a SUBSET of :semiconductor, so the distinct
  ;;   domain keys structurally PREVENT double-counting (G12).
  {:db/ident :compute.agg/id           :db/valueType :db.type/string  :db/unique :db.unique/identity :db/doc "e.g. \"agg.storage.exabytes.2024.shipped-capacity\""}
  {:db/ident :compute.agg/dimension    :db/valueType :db.type/keyword :db/doc ":domain | :geography"}
  {:db/ident :compute.agg/key          :db/valueType :db.type/keyword :db/doc "the dimension value, e.g. :storage or :world"}
  {:db/ident :compute.agg/year         :db/valueType :db.type/long    :db/doc "calendar year"}
  {:db/ident :compute.agg/metric       :db/valueType :db.type/keyword :db/doc "the aggregated metric, e.g. :shipped-capacity"}
  {:db/ident :compute.agg/unit         :db/valueType :db.type/keyword :db/doc "the common unit the Σ is in (aggregation never mixes units)"}
  {:db/ident :compute.agg/scale        :db/valueType :db.type/keyword :db/doc "the common scale the Σ is in (aggregation never mixes scales — TOP500 :petaflops is never summed with raw-FLOP :ones)"}
  {:db/ident :compute.agg/sum          :db/valueType :db.type/double  :db/doc "Σ across the series members in the graph for this (domain, unit, year) — bounded by coverage, NOT a market total (G12)"}
  {:db/ident :compute.agg/n            :db/valueType :db.type/long    :db/doc "number of series contributing (coverage denominator — read every aggregate against n; absence ≠ zero)"}
  {:db/ident :compute.agg/sourcing     :db/valueType :db.type/keyword :db/doc "always :synthesized"}]}
